===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*weh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|verray}}, from {{der|en|fro|verai|t=true}}, from {{der|en|la-eme|vērāgus}}, from {{der|en|CL.|vērāx}}, derived from {{m|la|vērus}}, from {{der|en|itc-pro|*wēros}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*weh₁ros}}.

Distantly cognate with the {{cog|ang|wǣr#Adjective_2|t=true}}. Over time displaced the use of a number of Germanic words or prefixes to convey the sense 'very' such as {{m|en|fele}}, {{m|ang|full-#Prefix_2}}, {{m|ang|mægen#Noun_2}}, {{m|enm|sore#Adverb_4}}, {{m|ang|sin-}}, {{m|en|swith#Adverb}}, (partially) {{m|enm|wel}}.

